						<td class="headline" align="left"><a name="#880">New Rules listing</a></td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td class="body">
							I'm posting the basics here, pending the addition of all the flowery words and stuff, but here is the core of what we have stood for and still stand for in Ancient Honor.<br />
<br />
Follow the Play Nice Rules.  If you don't know what they are, read them at www.everquest.com<br />
You can search the site and read them.  <br />
<br />
Cooperate with all other players, even if they're world-class jerks. Be firm in your dealings, but not rude.  There is nothing that can't be negotiated if you're willing to try.<br />
Remember, game time is too precious to waste arguing.<br />
<br />
<br />
Don't beg.  <br />
<br />
Begging from NPCs is a skill.  Begging from PCs is annoying. If you need to earn money, I or others in the guild can show or tell you how to make a small bundle.  Just ask how to make some plat, we'll point you in the right direction.<br />
  <br />
Borrowing from the guild treasury does not occur. Sorry, but no one wants to use their game time hunting down loans and I dont' want the accounting nightmare.  <br />
<br />
Don't spam us<br />
<br />
If you get an item, link it to us.  You might get a response if you want to sell it, but mostly we look at the itme for future reference.<br />
If you choose to start or join a private chat channel to sell your wares, that's cool.  <br />
<br />
Occasionally any of us will clean out our bank accounts and give away some of the stuff that's been gathering dust, and we may give away stuff what's in there. If you benefit from this, remember to give the item to some other guildy when you're done with it.<br />
<br />
Help each other<br />
<br />
If someone needs assistance, give it freely.  Don't put a burden of obligation on them for the help; give help willingly and with no strings.<br />
<br />
<br />
Help those who need it.<br />
<br />
If you're wandering around and see someone in trouble, stop and help.  Heal if you can, if not taunt the critter off the person---don't attack it, just stand there and absorb the aggro while they recover--or run away.  Carry extra food and drink for those who have none.  <br />
Our example is the Lone Ranger, who helps and then leaves people better than they were.  If you can rez, do so.  If you can heal, do it.  Helping just for the sake of helping is often a reward in itself.<br />
<br />
Group/guild functions<br />
<br />
We may have a group or get together with other guildies/guilds.  The r8ules will be posted before hand.  When you attend these, please be gracious winners and losers.  If you don't get the item you wanted, there's always another time.  <br />
<br />
There's more to follow, I'll get around ASAP, but generally the rule to follow is: if it feels wrong, it probably is!<br />
<br />
Ollie
